Package: GeoModelR
Title: Tools for the BayesTraits Geo Model — Palaeomap Preparation and Output Exploration
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jorge", "Avaria-Llautureo",
           email = "j.l.avaria@reading.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8610-7428"))
Description: GeoModelR provides tools for working with the Geographical (Geo)
    model implemented in BayesTraits v5+. The package covers two workflows:
    (1) Palaeomap preparation — downloading palaeocoastlines from the GPlates
    Web Service and exporting them as binary land/ocean CSV files and BuildMaps
    input files for BayesTraits; and (2) Output exploration — reading Geo model
    AncStates output files and visualising the posterior distribution of
    ancestral geographic coordinates on age-matched palaeomaps, including
    per-node, time-window, and clade-level plots.
    The package is linked to Avaria-Llautureo et al. (2025)
    <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2423833122>.
